Complete UV Python Project Tutorial
Beginner to Practical Project Development
1. What is UV?

UV is a modern, extremely fast Python package and project manager developed by Astral.

It helps you:

Create Python projects.
Create and manage virtual environments.
Install Python libraries.
Manage project dependencies.
Install Python versions.
Run Python programs.
Build and publish Python packages.

It combines many capabilities of tools such as pip, venv, and pip-tools.

2. Installing UV
Windows (PowerShell)
powershell
pip install uv


Alternatively, use the official installer:

powershell
powershell -ExecutionPolicy ByPass -c "irm https://astral.sh/uv/install.ps1 | iex"

Linux / macOS
bash
curl -LsSf https://astral.sh/uv/install.sh | sh

Verify Installation
bash
uv --version

3. Creating a New Python Project

Create a project named myproject:

bash
uv init myproject


Navigate into the project directory:

bash
cd myproject

Project Structure
text
myproject/
│
├── main.py
├── pyproject.toml
├── README.md
└── .python-version

main.py: Main Python application.
pyproject.toml: Project configuration and dependencies.
README.md: Project documentation.
.python-version: Specifies the Python version.
4. Creating a Virtual Environment

Run:

bash
uv venv


This creates a virtual environment named .venv.

Activate on Windows
powershell
.venv\Scripts\activate

Activate on Linux / macOS
bash
source .venv/bin/activate


Note: You do not need to activate the environment manually when using uv run.

5. Installing Python Libraries
Install a Single Library
bash
uv add fastapi

Install Multiple Libraries
bash
uv add fastapi pandas numpy requests

Install AI and Data Science Libraries
bash
uv add torch transformers datasets

Install RAG Project Libraries
bash
uv add qdrant-client sentence-transformers

Install Streamlit
bash
uv add streamlit

Remove a Library
bash
uv remove pandas

6. Running Python Programs

Run your Python file:

bash
uv run main.py


Check the Python version:

bash
uv run python --version


Open the Python interactive shell:

bash
uv run python

7. Important UV Commands
Command	Purpose
uv init	Create a new project
uv venv	Create a virtual environment
uv add package	Install a package
uv remove package	Remove a package
uv sync	Synchronize dependencies
uv run main.py	Run a Python file
uv lock	Update the lock file
uv tree	Display dependency tree
uv pip list	List installed packages
uv python list	List available Python versions
uv python install 3.12	Install Python 3.12
uv build	Build the project
uv self update	Update UV
uv cache clean	Clear the UV cache
uv --help	Display help
8. Practical Project: Building a FastAPI Backend

Let's create a simple backend application using UV.

Step 1: Create a Project
bash
uv init ai-project
cd ai-project

Step 2: Install FastAPI and Uvicorn
bash
uv add fastapi uvicorn

Step 3: Write Code in main.py
python
from fastapi import FastAPI

app = FastAPI()

@app.get("/")
def home():
    return {
        "message": "My AI Project is Running!"
    }

Step 4: Run the Server
bash
uv run uvicorn main:app --reload

Step 5: Open in Your Browser

Application URL:

text
http://127.0.0.1:8000


API Documentation:

text
http://127.0.0.1:8000/docs


Congratulations! Your first FastAPI backend is ready.

